rekindle-media-bwe
==================

This crate contains code copied from str0m, a Sans-I/O WebRTC implementation
in Rust:

  Project:   str0m (https://github.com/algesten/str0m)
  Revision:  393a3d23 (release 0.24.1; str0m-proto 0.7.0)
  Licence:   MIT OR Apache-2.0, used here under the MIT licence (below)

Copied paths (str0m repository -> this crate)
---------------------------------------------

  src/bwe/                           -> src/bwe/
    mod.rs, acked_bitrate_estimator.rs, link_capacity_estimator.rs,
    loss_controller.rs, macros.rs, smoother.rs, time.rs,
    alr_detector/{mod,budget,detector}.rs,
    delay/{mod,arrival_group,control,rate_control,trendline}.rs,
    probe/{mod,cluster,control,estimator}.rs
    (src/bwe/api.rs is not copied: it is the facade over str0m's `Rtc`)
  src/pacer/                         -> src/pacer/
    mod.rs, control.rs, leaky.rs, null.rs, queue.rs
  src/streams/send_queue.rs          -> src/pacer/send_queue.rs
  crates/proto/src/bandwidth.rs      -> src/bandwidth.rs (Bitrate, DataSize)
  src/rtp/id.rs                      -> src/twcc.rs (TwccSeq, TwccClusterId, num_id!)
  src/rtp/rtcp/twcc.rs               -> src/twcc.rs (TwccPacketId, TwccSendRecord,
                                        TwccRecvReport)
  src/util/mod.rs                    -> src/util/mod.rs (Soonest)
  src/util/time_tricks.rs            -> src/util/time_tricks.rs (not_happening,
                                        already_happened)
  src/util/average.rs                -> src/util/average.rs (MovingAverage)
  src/lib.rs                         -> src/reason.rs (Reason, pacer/bwe variants),
                                        src/lib.rs (log_stat!)

Changes
-------

The changes are mechanical adaptation only. The algorithms, constants and unit
tests are str0m's. Specifically:

  - Module paths and visibility (`pub(crate)` -> `pub` where the public API
    needs it; `pub(super)` where a file was split).
  - The pacer identifies a queue by `QueueId(u32)` instead of the RTP
    `MidRid`; `SendQueue` is generic over the packet type instead of holding
    `RtpPacket`s.
  - `TwccSendRecord::new` and `TwccRecvReport::new` are public constructors
    (str0m builds records only inside its RTCP TWCC register, which is not
    copied); `LeakyBucketPacer::set_queue_limit` sets the existing queue-limit
    field, which str0m keeps at its 2 s default.
  - Rust `as` casts are replaced by functions in src/util/num.rs that return
    the same value as the cast for every input; `#[allow(...)]` attributes are
    removed by equivalent rewrites (an unused field and an unused parameter
    dropped, a boxed enum variant, merged identical match arms, `vec![]`
    literals in tests, a no-op stats macro that type-checks its arguments
    without evaluating them).
  - Signature-only lint fixes: `PacerControl::calculate` and the loss
    controller's `get_loss_probability` are associated functions (str0m takes
    `&self` and never reads it); `PartialObservation::update` borrows its
    summary; `Instant`/`Duration` subtraction uses `checked_sub(..).unwrap()`
    (the same panic on underflow).
  - Files over 600 lines are split into submodules; test modules moved into
    their own files.
  - Renames: str0m's private `bwe::time::Timestamp` is `BweTimestamp`, and a
    few private fields and test-only fields were renamed for lints.

